  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**opentelemetry-operator** turns the `OpenTelemetryCollector` resources in `helm-charts/opentelemetry/opentelemetry-raw`\ninto DaemonSets/Deployments, Services and ServiceMonitors, and serves admission webhooks (validation/defaulting of\ncollector CRs, pod mutation for SDK auto-instrumentation). If it fails, running collectors keep running but\n**config changes are not applied**.\n\n**OBI** (OpenTelemetry eBPF Instrumentation, DaemonSet `obi`) attaches eBPF probes to processes in the namespaces of\nits `instrumented-namespaces` rule (`staffops*`) and sends traces/metrics to the node's otel-agent. Its health is\nvisible on the *OpenTelemetry Collectors* dashboard as data received by otel-agent; here only its CPU/memory.\n\n**Healthy**: operator up and leader, reconcile errors 0, work queue drains to 0, webhook 5xx ~0.\n\n**When red**\n- *Reconcile errors* (chart alert ReconcileErrors: any error rate over 5m) \u2192 `kubectl --context k8s01 -n opentelemetry logs deploy/opentelemetry-operator`; usually an invalid collector config.\n- *Webhook 5xx* \u2192 Argo CD syncs of collector CRs fail; check the webhook certificate (cert-manager).\n- *OBI memory near its 1 GiB limit* \u2192 too many instrumented processes / connections.\n\nMetric reference: [controller-runtime](https://book.kubebuilder.io/reference/metrics-reference).",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext"
        }
      },
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Overview",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "id": 2,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      }
